Reiterating that the illegal exploitation and trade of natural resources, including coltan from mining areas in North Kivu, continues to fuel armed conflict and finance illicit armed groups in eastern DRC, and emphasizing the need to track and disrupt illicit financial flows derived from such exploitation in order to address the root causes of the conflict,

1. Condemns in the strongest terms the military offensive and territorial expansion of the M23 in North Kivu and South Kivu, and demands that the M23 immediately cease all hostilities, halt its advance, and withdraw completely and unconditionally from all occupied territories, in accordance with the decisions taken within the framework of the Luanda and Nairobi processes;

2. Demands the immediate cessation of all external support to the M23 and any other armed group operating in the DRC, demands the immediate withdrawal of all unauthorized foreign military forces, personnel, and equipment from the territory of the DRC, and explicitly calls upon the Government of Rwanda to immediately withdraw all its military personnel, military assets, and surface-to-air missile systems from the territory of the DRC;

3. Calls upon the Government of the DRC to immediately put an end to any cooperation, coordination, or provision of support by the FARDC to armed groups, in particular the FDLR, and to implement without delay the FDLR neutralization plan agreed under the Luanda process;

