6. Reaffirms its full support for MONUSCO and SAMIDRC in the execution of their mandates, recalls the provisions of resolution 2746 (2024) regarding MONUSCO’s support to SAMIDRC, stresses the imperative of protecting peacekeepers, underscores the necessity of bringing to justice and holding accountable all perpetrators of attacks against United Nations and regional personnel, demands that all parties cease any obstruction or intimidation against United Nations and regional personnel, and reiterates its readiness to consider targeted sanctions against individuals and entities threatening the peace, security, or stability of the DRC, including those providing support to armed groups such as the M23, those attacking peacekeepers, and those involved in the illicit exploitation and trafficking of natural resources;

7. Calls upon the DRC and Rwanda to urgently de-escalate tensions, restore diplomatic dialogue, and re-engage in good faith under the mediation of Angola within the framework of the Luanda process, commends the ongoing efforts of the African Union and regional partners to restore peace and stability, reaffirms its support for African solutions to African problems, and calls upon the international community to assist the countries of the region in addressing the root causes of conflict through dialogue, mutual respect, and sustainable development;

